    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nSo I co-maintain a plugin for autosaving (see https://github.com/okuuva/auto-save.nvim). One functionality we offer is to provide a `defer_save` and a `cancel_deferred_save` action. Each of these gets a list of events. When one of these events trigger the action is triggered.\r\nAs you might guess, `defer_save` defers a save to be run in the future, where as `cancel_deferred_save` cancels a pending save. By default the events are:\r\n```lua\r\n    defer_save = { \"InsertLeave\", \"TextChanged\" },\r\n    cancel_deferred_save = { \"InsertEnter\" },\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow we had users report a weird thing. When pressing `<CR>` betwen e.g. `{}` in insert mode, a save would be deferred. We realized it is because of this plugin, since it remaps `<CR>` in these situations. I'm not sure what happens but it looks it triggers `\"InsertLeave\"` but won't trigger `\"InsertEnter\"`, because of this code: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.pairs/blob/694d9beb488ff1afaf3d1977b067e53c827d9af5/lua/mini/pairs.lua#L398\r\nIn the end it leads to an unexpected save confuses the user.\r\n\r\nHow could we go on with this? User @akikanellis showed some solutions here: https://github.com/okuuva/auto-save.nvim/issues/57#issuecomment-2322882389 . Maybe you could give some feedback.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n \r\nI will provide one if needed, but I think it's more of a technical problem.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n?",
