            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\n> I'm not sure what happens but it looks it triggers `\"InsertLeave\"` but won't trigger `\"InsertEnter\"`, because of this code: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.pairs/blob/694d9beb488ff1afaf3d1977b067e53c827d9af5/lua/mini/pairs.lua#L398\r\n\r\nThis code prevents listed events from being triggered during execution of `<C-o>` which accompanies `<CR>` . See 2049bca9c51214ef61a9c29e05cc7ef82556840b for more details.\r\n\r\nBoth in tests and right interactively I can not reproduce the \"... it triggers `\"InsertLeave\"` but won't trigger `\"InsertEnter\"` ...\" part. Typing in Insert mode `<CR>` with cursor inside `{}` and 'mini.pairs' set up *does not* trigger any of the listed there events. Entering and exiting Insert mode with a regular `i` and `<Esc>` still work as expected. So I would need a reproduction example here, please (with latest `main` branch, of course).",
